# Local settings. Copy to the repo root as .env (`task setup` does it for you).
# NEVER commit a real .env.
#
# Who reads this file:
#   - docker compose, to fill in ${...} values in docker-compose.yml
#   - task, so the addresses it prints match your ports
#   - `flask` in host mode (no Docker), which loads the nearest .env
#
# Everything is commented out: the defaults already work on a Mac, in the
# devcontainer and in Codespaces. Uncomment a line only to change it.

# Flask secret + JWT signing key. The dev default is fine on your own machine.
# For anything shared, use a long random value, e.g.
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# SECRET_KEY=

# Host ports: the page (split origin), the AWS-shaped edge (one origin), the API.
# If you move API_PORT, point front-end/js/config.js at it too.
# WEB_PORT=5500
# EDGE_PORT=8080
# API_PORT=5050

# Which page addresses may call the API from another port (split-origin CORS).
# Default: http://127.0.0.1 or http://localhost on port 5500 or 5501.
# Setting a single address here replaces that pattern.
# CORS_ORIGIN=
